  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "The Padres led after three innings, then the game got away in the fourth. V\u00e1squez couldn't hold it. The bullpen hemorrhaged. It was the kind of loss that compounds. Not because they played bad baseball early, but because they played good baseball and still lost. This is what slipping looks like. You get your chances, you don't finish, and six games later you're still looking for the win that stops it.",
    "what_this_means": "Cronenworth kept them relevant. He drove in three runs. The lineup scraped together ten hits. They scored in the first, they scored in the second, and that should have been enough. But the pitching inverted after the third. Wandy Peralta gave up four in one inning. The game turned in one stretch, the kind of stretch that doesn't come back. This team has inconsistency wired into its DNA. Balanced production one moment, chaos the next. They had the lead. They didn't finish with it. Thirteen games back, and the margin just got wider.",
    "what_to_watch": "Shohei Ohtani brings a 1.58 ERA tonight. Michael King is your answer.",
